rules:
- id: preserve-stack-trace
  patterns:
  - pattern-inside: |
      try {
        ...
      } catch ($TYPE $EXCEPTION) {
        $BODY
      }
  - pattern: |
      throw $EXPR;
  - pattern-not: |
      throw new $EXCEPTION_TYPE(...);
  - pattern-not: |
      throw $EXCEPTION.initCause(...);
  - pattern-not: |
      throw $EXCEPTION.fillInStackTrace();
  - pattern-not: |
      throw $EXCEPTION.getTargetException();
  - pattern-not: |
      throw $EXCEPTION.getCause();
  - pattern-not: |
      throw $EXCEPTION.getException();
  message: |
    Preserve original stack trace when rethrowing exceptions. When rethrowing an exception you should take care to preserve the original stack trace by either:
    1) Passing the original exception to the new exception constructor, or
    2) Using initCause() to set the original exception as the cause
  languages: [java]
  severity: WARNING
  metadata:
    category: best-practices
    subcategory: error-handling
    cwe:
    - 'CWE-705: Incorrect Control Flow Scoping'
    references:
    - https://wiki.sei.cmu.edu/confluence/display/java/ERR07-J.+Do+not+throw+RuntimeException%2C+Exception%2C+or+Throwable
    owasp:
    - A10:2021 - Security Logging and Monitoring Failures
